{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration and obstacle-recovery policy in compact deterministic specifications. The policy gives strong forward bias in clear space, uses one-shot recovery actions after obstacle events, keeps uncontrollable events total in every spec state, treats obstacle events as safety-critical preemptions in action states, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated last-resort path after repeated front blockage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensor outcomes and motion capabilities into plant automata so specifications can bind perception to exactly one safe action per decision state.",
    "Use clear-space alternation between move_forward and occasional random_walk for coverage, directed turns for side obstacles, brief backward escape only for front blockage, and full_rotate only from a dedicated stuck state after repeated failed front recovery."
  ],
